notes={
362203:('parked_source_scope','Conjecture 2; Definition 3; conclusion. Odd-order Buekenhout–Metz unitals are proved in the source. The target quantifies over every nonclassical embedded unital, including other families.','No finite-geometry enumeration: no independently validated catalogue of the remaining embedded unitals was obtained.','Construct or certify a non-BM unital of order q>5 and test every six-line configuration, or prove a universal incidence theorem.','High: field/plane incidence semantics and a large complete nonexistence certificate.'),
362204:('parked_structural','Conjecture 1.12, Definition 1.8, Theorem 1.11 in current v2. Graphs may have parallel edges; sparse condition must use the source nonempty-subgraph convention. Known range d<=2(k+1) is not new. Mies thesis found in citing search retains the remaining strong problem.','No new exhaustive multigraph decomposition search. Small simple graphs with n<=d+1 cannot test the difficult component-size regime meaningfully.','Find a (k,d)-sparse multigraph with d>2(k+1), no overfull subgraph, and certify infeasibility of all forest decompositions.','Medium certificate cost, high discovery cost.'),
362205:('parked_structural','Source Conjecture 1.20, Theorems 1.18–1.19 and thin-tree discussion. Forest plus components of at most four edges is known; replacing that forest by stars is additional.','No planar census or exact forest/star partition enumeration completed.','Produce a planar girth>=5 graph with a complete partition obstruction, or strengthen the discharging/exchange theorem.','Medium: explicit embedding/girth and partition checker.'),
362310:('parked_after_structured_search','Section 2 rooted products and G_c(s,t); Lemma 4.1 cases (i)–(iii), proof inequalities; final Conjecture 4.1. Rooted tree bases used have root degree exactly c, hence split into the required c pendant-root branches.','2,292 floating spectral comparisons, k=2,3, base trees order 4–14, c=2–4, (s,t)=(2,2),(3,2),(3,3),(4,2),(4,3),(4,4). No reversal. Closest gap about 0.2393. See logs/graft.log. Not exhaustive and not a certified real interval calculation.','Extend the source mass-difference estimate beyond its three hypotheses; alternatively find a genuinely different rooted connected attachment giving a strict reverse inequality and certify it exactly.','Medium/high: literal distance and Perron eigenvalue comparison.'),
362340:('parked_definition_mismatch','Source Conjecture 1.1 is ordinary odd coloring: each nonisolated vertex has SOME color occurring oddly in its neighborhood. MathDB instead says EVERY present color, the strong odd-coloring condition. The intended planar odd-5 target is retained.','No attempt to count a refutation of the stronger paraphrase; bounded recent literature search still discusses ordinary odd-5 as a conjecture.','Resolve ordinary odd-5 for all planar graphs; a strong-odd counterexample does not qualify.','High discovery difficulty, medium finite certificate if one exists.'),
362341:('excluded_routine_source_mechanism','Source Section 3 defines K_n^* by one subdivision per edge; Conjecture 4.2 excludes K_(n+1)^* as a subgraph. The same degree-2 forcing works for every subdivided graph.','Definition-level exact diagnostic for the Mycielski graph of K9: 19 vertices, 117 edges, no K10. Its subdivision is biplanar and forces at least 10 odd colors, with no K10^*. See ROUTES.md.','No research candidate: this is an elementary classical construction combined with the source own subdivision mechanism, expressly excluded by campaign rules.','Low, but prohibited significance profile.'),
362342:('excluded_published_solution','Literal record and source introduction explicitly report analytical proof by Mao and combinatorial proof by Yee. Search also found the stronger Merca proof arXiv:2411.13818.','No heavy search; already settled.','None eligible: formalizing an already known theorem earns zero.','Irrelevant after novelty exclusion.'),
362378:('parked_topological','Current source v2, simple-drawing definitions and plane Hamiltonian discussion; citing Aichholzer–Orthaber–Vogtenhuber separable-drawings paper proves the property for that class, not all simple drawings.','No complete rotation-system/crossing realizability enumeration. Straight-line point sets would test a known subclass only.','Find a realizable simple drawing with prescribed endpoints and a complete noncrossing Hamilton-path obstruction; abstract crossing patterns alone are inadequate.','High semantic cost for topological drawing realizability.'),
362434:('parked_after_extended_exact_search','Definition 2.7 angle-rigidity matrix [R M], Theorem 3.5, Conjecture 3.6, Proposition 3.2 counterexamples, Section 4.1 verified range. Current v2 retains conjecture. New arXiv:2611.02764 concerns subtended/global angle and bearing constraints; its abstract is not an identification with this colored-angle matroid.','20,000 sampled colored graphs orders 4–8, then 500 each at orders 9–12 with 2–4 colors. Exact modular row rank at integer points; deficient samples tested by literal rainbow-deletion plus Laman subset inequalities. No sample satisfied the conjectured condition while remaining rank-deficient. Modular deficiency is diagnostic, not proof of generic dependence.','For a counterexample prove symbolic generic rank deficiency, independently verify every color transversal requirement, and eliminate all printed figure/gadget augmentations. For a positive theorem prove the converse of Theorem 3.5.','Medium for finite polynomial certificate, high for full theorem.'),
362437:('parked_after_two_search_families','Source Section 3 defines distance redundancy via unique two-walks; Section 7 gives selection by number of degree-2 neighbors then degree, minimum-cardinality fill and subsequent deletions. Section 4.2 disconnected weak graphs allowed but isolated vertices are not. Lemma 4.5 is not used as an executable substitute for the distance definition.','1,950 cycle-seeded weak-graph trials, orders 6–18, followed by 45,000 independent random simple graph draws, orders 10–18; 50 of those were weak. Exact min-fill and spanning weak-subgraph deletion search; explicit unknown caps retained. No certified failure. Refinement filters fills to edges incident with a degree deficit; same outcomes. A third independent 1,200-trial sample of cycle-seeded graphs of orders 11–18, using randomized deletion witnesses before exact recursion, all passed; it does not resolve the earlier capped graph instances.','Resolve capped subgraph searches and selection quantifiers (some/every eligible vertex and some/every minimum fill), or discover a failure beyond the source tested orders and prove it is not a printed obstruction modification.','Low/medium for explicit adjacency and complete finite reduction obstruction.'),
362452:('parked_parametric_sdp','Source Section 1.2, Conjecture 1.3, finite proved k=2–5 cases; search retained Cohn/de Laat/Leijenhorst and associated exact-SDP literature.','No new SDP computation: k=2–5 are already established, while k=6 requires a new sharp parametric or large exact SDP certificate.','Uniform exact positive-semidefinite dual certificate for all k>=2, including semantic link to three-point bounds.','High: SDP positivity and spherical-code semantics.'),
362480:('parked_after_exhaustive_search','Source Conjecture 1.1 uses sums mod 3. West historical page states connected-graph version and notes connectedness may be unnecessary; current source explicitly states all graphs. Classic families and cordiality exclusion precedent retained.','Every labeled simple graph of orders 1–7 tested exactly, including disconnected graphs; at order 7 all 2,097,152 graphs pass, using 105 balanced vertex partitions up to color permutation. See logs/cordial.log. No multigraph claim.','A new non-3-cordial simple graph with exhaustive labeling certificate or a full-scope theorem distinct from known cordiality reductions.','Low finite-certificate cost; no discovered witness.'),
362504:('parked_analytic','Primary source positive Dirac eigenvalue conventions and ratio optimization/numerical-shape discussion; mass and boundary regularity matter. Abstract text has minimize/maximize ambiguity, so no claim from that wording.','No numerical shape optimization: would not certify the operator eigenvalue ratio or the entire admissible-domain class.','A rigorous domain/eigenvalue comparison for the intended ratio problem, not a paraphrase/domain defect.','Very high analytic formalization cost.'),
362571:('excluded_endpoint_source_formula','Source Conjecture 21 prints n>=5; author Shankar slides state n>5. Signed-excedance formula appears in source. Independent enumeration of all 120 permutations at n=5 gives even polynomial 1+11t+36t²+11t³+t⁴.','Exact integer Sturm calculation gives no real roots for the even polynomial; direct reciprocal-square identity proves positivity. This is a smallest-parameter/source-formula correction, not an eligible discovery.','Intended n>5 problem remains unproved here. No candidate and no Lean investment in the endpoint error.','Low for defect, but zero credit.'),
362623:('excluded_refuted_in_current_source','Current arXiv v3, Conjecture 3.2 and Remark 3.3: all subsets of k directions must have total at least 2^k. Source cites earlier Gray-code literature and notes a corrected sufficient condition for large dimension.','Tuple (2,2,2,10,16) in dimension 5 satisfies the printed individual bounds and sum but fails the three-coordinate projection bound, 6<8. It is direct application of the source own remark.','No eligible new result for printed target; no adjacent corrected conjecture pursued.','Low but excluded.'),
362703:('parked_after_small_exact_search','Source Conjecture 2.6 and Proposition 2.7: small-quasikernel conjecture implies large neighborhood version; generalized-q-kernel citing work located.','All loopless labeled digraphs through order 4 including digons checked exactly: 1,4,64,4096 objects; no failure.','A new obstruction or an extremal structural theorem beyond the source reduction. Small diagnostic does not settle this famous target.','Low for witness, high for full theorem.'),
362706:('parked_after_small_exact_search','Source structural dichotomy in concluding discussion: large induced acyclic set or high-outdegree vertex belonging to a quasikernel. Uses outward reachability convention.','Same complete digraph census through order 4; all subsets and quasikernels checked. Square comparisons implement sqrt(n) thresholds exactly. No failure.','Prove the structural dichotomy uniformly or give complete finite obstruction satisfying source conventions.','Low finite certificate, high discovery difficulty.'),
362708:('parked_classical_bridge_risk','Source Conjecture 3.40 and Remark 3.41 already provide the four-shape inclusion and explicitly propose excluding other shapes using f^lambda>n(n-3)/2. Rasala minimal-degree results (1977), quoted in a primary 2015 paper Lemma 3.1, fit this remaining strategy.','Exact hook-length dimensions for every partition at n=5 and 9<=n<=45; no extra shape of dimension <=n(n-3)/2 beyond (n),(n-1,1),(n-2,2) and their conjugates. Dominance excludes the first two row shapes. No all-n equality-classification proof was rebuilt.','Need precise Rasala equality-shape classification and full all-n bridge; even if completed this is at strong risk of being an excluded classical theorem plus the source explicit strategy, not significant new mathematics.','High literal Kostka/Schur semantics, poor novelty profile.'),
362744:('parked_association_schemes','Source Conjecture 31.4 (journal Conjecture 206); diameter>=3, Q-polynomial primitive idempotent, Norton-balanced configuration, constant kite function. Current v2 and journal search retain this statement.','No classification or exact distance-regular graph enumeration. Testing familiar schemes would revisit source families.','Construct a Norton-balanced Q-polynomial graph with nonconstant zeta_i, or prove the structural implication; all idempotent/Norton semantics required.','Very high algebraic-combinatorial semantic cost.'),
362748:('parked_universal_algebra','Source Conjecture 34 and equivalent projective-core statement. NEQ_k is disequality ON a k-element domain, not a k-ary relation as the MathDB prose says. Theorem 23 covers <=7 vertices; journal metadata confirms 2025 publication.','No search beyond seven: binary/ternary product polymorphism spaces require a sound CSP/clone checker, not just ordinary graph endomorphism testing.','An indecomposable connected core of order>=8 with certified failure of the disequality pp-definition/projectivity equivalence, or a full proof of that equivalence.','High semantics; endomorphism-only certificates would be insufficient.')}
