summary=['# Expanded corpus r225\n','No qualifying new solution or literal Lean endpoint was obtained. All 20 reserved IDs have explicit dispositions in `results.json`; four routes are excluded and sixteen are parked. No acceptance or ledger change is claimed.\n','## Source and prior-art work\n','All 20 exact raw JSONL records, trailing newline, one-based source line, chunk/raw/statement hashes are preserved in `raw/` and `extracted.json`. Ancestor AGENTS, lane TASK (including `python3 -I -B`), current and inherited ledgers and accepted/excluded-family precedents were read. Historical search outputs are retained. Current abstract pages and every version listed there were retrieved with append-only HTTP receipts. Primary-source text is in `sources/`; example/figure caption inventory is `source-example-inventory.json`. Figure geometry was not visually audited. Literature searches preceded numerical searches; bounded results are retained as `sources/web-search-*.json`.\n','Live GitHub heads and path trees were fetched for Lean Pool, OpenAI/math and Omega. OpenAI and Omega root trees are truncated; a separate full OpenAI preprints tree and overview were fetched. No semantic or worldwide novelty clearance is claimed. Denied Crossref, Semantic Scholar, arXiv search API, ScienceDirect, DBLP and inherited MathDB routes were not directly requested. Search engines sometimes returned snippets from denied domains; these were not followed. No TLS bypass, browser tab, upload, external message, git operation, child agent, or write outside this lane was used.\n','## Mathematical outcomes\n']
for i,(status,review,attempt,gap,cost) in notes.items():summary.append(f'- **{i} — {status}.** {attempt}\n')
summary+=['\n## Reproduction and limits\n','Scripts use the standard library and real lane-local paths, invoked with `python3 -I -B`. Numerical work used `scripts/limited.py`: 2-CPU affinity, CPU 120 s, wall 140 s, sampled 6 GiB RSS cap, MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2; full logs and receipts are in `logs/`. Only one expensive process ran at a time. Small definition-level checks were brief. RSS monitoring is sampled per process, not a cgroup guarantee. The C++ version of the weak search was not compiled because g++ was unavailable; a separate Python implementation ran instead. That unused source is retained, with no execution claim. No packages were installed.\n','This is a bounded investigation with sustained finite attempts, not exhaustive resolution or the requested several-hour comprehensive pass. Unexecuted proposed searches and remaining semantic/literature barriers are explicit per ID. No dummy Lean endpoint was generated, and no upstream rebuild or Lean axiom audit is claimed. `CANDIDATE.md` explains why there is no qualifying candidate; `ROUTES.md` records the excluded elementary arguments and diagnostic semantics.\n']
(D/'SUMMARY.md').write_text('\n'.join(summary))
(D/'CANDIDATE.md').write_text('''# No qualifying candidate\n\nZero new exact solutions are submitted for acceptance, and no Lean packet is claimed.\n\nThe strongest explored finite routes were 362434 (angle rigidity), 362437 (partial-short weak graph reduction), and 362310 (graft spectral radius). Their bounded searches found no qualifying witness. Capped cases are unresolved. The immersion interval route 362708 follows the source’s explicit low-dimension strategy and appears to be a short bridge from classical minimal-degree classification, with a remaining equality-classification source check; it is not advanced as a new theorem.\n\n362341 has an elementary classical Mycielski/subdivision refutation, 362571 has a smallest-parameter error computed from the source’s own formula (also corrected in author slides), 362623 is contradicted by the source’s own current remark, and 362342 is already published. These cannot earn campaign credit.\n\nDo not invest Lean capacity in the excluded routes. A future continuation should first resolve the remaining literature/semantic gaps in results.json, then improve the exact weak-subgraph and colored-angle searches. None of the finite positive diagnostics is a proof of a universal conjecture.\n''')
